# "Evoke - Exile a red card from your hand" (CR 118.9, 702.74): on turn 1 Bot1's hand is Fury and six Mountains - no other red
# card - so the evoke way is not offered (a Mountain is colorless; Fury itself cannot pay for itself). On turn 3 it has drawn a
# Lightning Bolt and evokes Fury exiling it (the positive control). Bot2 controls no creature or planeswalker. The damage ability may choose no targets (CR 107.1c); the evoke trigger still sacrifices Fury.

[Bot1 Deck]
Fury
Mountain x6
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
! Bot1.Hand.Fury.Cast(Ability: Evoke)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Fury.Cast(Ability: Evoke)
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Graveyard = Fury
Stack.Count = 0
